%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dctcp-receiver -- a DCTCP receiver acknowledges at once when the CE state of the arriving data changes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of DcTcp (RFC 8257 section 3.2): "If the CE codepoint is set and
DCTCP.CE is false, set DCTCP.CE to true and send an immediate ACK", and the same when CE is
clear and DCTCP.CE is true.

The class dctcp-receiver: DcTcp::processEcnInEstablished() sets ack_now at each change of the
CE state. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "dctcp" from the other algorithms, which delay the ACK of
the marked segment.

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp and the delayed ACK (the default), which listens at the
port 1000; host2 connects with classic ECN (tcpEcnMode "rfc3168") and sends 30000 bytes at
0.2 s, and the tap marks the 5th data segment of host2 CE. Observation: level 1, host1 sends no
ACK of exactly three segments, as the delayed ACK of unmarked data, and then an ACK of exactly
five segments.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dctcp-receiver
%# value: "DcTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReceiver")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn2} + 1 + 4 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .set("ipv4.ecn", "3")
                     .describe("the 5th data segment of host2: mark it CE"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host2")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 1 + 3 * 1448")
                             .describe("an ACK of exactly three segments: no delayed ACK")
                             .within(1.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 1 + 5 * 1448")
             .describe("the ACK of host1 of exactly five segments")
             .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReceiver compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpEchoApp"
*.host1.app[0].localPort = 1000
*.host1.app[0].echoFactor = 0
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host2.app[0].connectAddress = "host1"
*.host2.app[0].connectPort = 1000
*.host2.app[0].tOpen = 0.1s
*.host2.app[0].tSend = 0.2s
*.host2.app[0].sendBytes = 30000B
*.host2.app[0].tClose = 1000s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpReceiver: PASS
